(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103: a buffer CAN be changed in place, so a text
 field written from one takes a copy of its bytes, the same copy a text
 variable takes. Rewriting a byte, clearing, appending to and freeing the
 buffer afterwards leaves the field as it was written.)

A thing called note has
  a text called body is "".

a buffer called scratch is 16 bytes in size.
copy "cat" to scratch.
a note called saved.
Set saved's body to scratch.
Set byte 1 of scratch to 98.
Print saved's body.
Print scratch.
clear scratch.
append "something else" to scratch.
Print saved's body.
Free scratch.
Print saved.
